      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8fc1e37e",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image displays a man (actor Mike Myers) with a stern, unimpressed facial expression, juxtaposed with text stating 'there was a 4 car pile-up in mexico' and 'today 93 people died'. The intent is to use the actor's expression as a visual punchline to mock or trivialize a tragic real-world event — a fatal car accident in Mexico. This is harmful because it reduces a serious, life-altering tragedy to a joke, potentially desensitizing viewers to human suffering and implying that such events are somehow humorous or inconsequential. The meme does not target any specific group based on protected characteristics, but its core intent is to inflict emotional harm by mocking the gravity of the situation, which can be seen as a form of emotional abuse or disrespect toward victims and their families. The overall intent is to provoke laughter at the expense of human loss, which is inherently harmful.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2ccbe2e1"
      },
